Privacy Policy for Plate Quest

Last updated: October 4, 2026

This privacy policy applies to the Plate Quest mobile application for Android.

1. Data Collection and Usage

Plate Quest does not collect, store, share, or transmit any personally identifiable information (PII) or user data to external servers or third parties.

The application functions entirely offline. All game data, including gameplay progress, saved games, scores, and preferences, is stored strictly on your local device (via your device's local application storage).

2. Device Permissions

Plate Quest requires no sensitive device permissions. It does not access your location, camera, microphone, contacts, storage files, or phone state.

3. Third-Party Services & Advertising

Plate Quest does not contain any advertisements, third-party trackers, analytics SDKs, or third-party payment processors.

4. Children's Privacy

Because Plate Quest does not collect any personal information whatsoever, it is safe for users of all ages, including children under 13.

5. Changes to This Privacy Policy

If we update this privacy policy in the future, the updated policy will be posted within our app documentation or updates.

